      "name": "Harbor Trust letter",
      "description": "A letter from the Calder Harbor Trust Company dated 11 October 1948, asking Mr. Edmund Ashgrove to kindly confirm his personal guarantee, signed 2 August, of a $40,000 loan to Whitlock Holdings. A photostat of the guarantee is pinned to it; the signature 'Edmund Ashgrove' is careful and a little too round. In the margin, in Edmund's spiky pencil: 'NOT MY HAND. Harrow - Monday.' You know the name: Inspector Harrow runs the fraud squad at headquarters.",
      "found_in": "study",
