      "name": "Gap in the medicine cabinet",
      "description": "On the top shelf of Edmund's bathroom cabinet, a clean ring in the dust where a small bottle stood, beside its pharmacist's carton: 'Digitalis tincture, 30 ml. E. Ashgrove. Ten drops at night. Filled 14 Oct. 1948, Mercer's Pharmacy.' A bottle filled two days ago would be nearly full. It is gone, and this room is a minute up the back stairs from the hall passage.",
