      "name": "Bottle in a handkerchief",
      "description": "Dug out of the disturbed soil of the conservatory palm: a small brown pharmacy bottle, empty, labeled 'Digitalis tincture - E. Ashgrove - Mercer's Pharmacy', wrapped in a white linen handkerchief embroidered 'S.W.' in blue thread at one corner. The neck still smells bitter. Somebody carried Edmund's heart drops down from his bathroom and buried them here in a handkerchief marked with those initials.",
