          "condition": "pressed"
        },
        {
          "clue_id": "vance-raised-voices",
          "text": "Says that at about 20:20, waiting in the hall for his appointment, he heard Clara and Edmund shouting in the study. He caught only one word clearly, in Clara's voice: 'regret'.",
          "condition": "pressed"
        },
        {
          "clue_id": "vance-dead-line",
          "text": "Says that at about half past eight, still waiting in the hall, he watched Edmund come out of the study, lift the hall telephone, rattle the hook and mutter 'Dead. The storm.' Edmund glanced at the hall clock and wrote something on the message pad before calling him in for their meeting.",
          "condition": "pressed"
        }
      ],
      "breaks_on": ["draft-codicil"],
      "patience": 13,
      "deflections": [
        "*polishes his spectacles with a folded handkerchief*  Strictly speaking, Detective, I am not obliged to speculate.",
